1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,028
For a child with mosaic variegated aneuploidy, a plausible
medicine is only a starting point.

2
00:00:06,028 --> 00:00:12,427
We propose arimoclomol for laboratory testing, with
explicit rules for deciding whether it deserves to
advance.

3
00:00:12,427 --> 00:00:15,762
We have not demonstrated drug rescue or treated this
child.

4
00:00:15,762 --> 00:00:20,901
Our contribution is a testable proposal, supported by
working tools that others can use.

5
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:30,802
The two identified variants affect the gene that makes Bub
R one, a protein involved in chromosome separation.

6
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:31,962
Their phase is inferred.

7
00:00:31,962 --> 00:00:34,839
The exact protein consequences remain unmeasured.

8
00:00:34,839 --> 00:00:40,471
The missense variant could reduce abundance, impair
function, do both, or remain indeterminate.

9
00:00:40,471 --> 00:00:45,255
The proposed experiment compares full-length normal and
altered protein at matched abundance.

10
00:00:45,255 --> 00:00:48,757
An isolated fragment's melting curve cannot settle that
question.

11
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,749
The protocol has four gates.

12
00:00:53,749 --> 00:00:58,362
Gate A establishes the variant's effect using full-length
protein at matched abundance.

13
00:00:58,362 --> 00:01:01,992
Gate B qualifies measurement, pathway response and
exposure.

14
00:01:01,992 --> 00:01:06,848
Gate C measures chromosome segregation while separately
tracking division and cell fate.

15
00:01:06,848 --> 00:01:09,731
Gate D applies prespecified confidence bounds.

16
00:01:09,731 --> 00:01:11,500
More protein alone cannot pass.

17
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,372
Neither can apparent improvement from stopping division or
selectively losing abnormal cells.

18
00:01:16,372 --> 00:01:18,184
Failed controls are indeterminate.

19
00:01:18,184 --> 00:01:21,722
An interval touching the worthwhile-benefit threshold is
inconclusive.

20
00:01:21,722 --> 00:01:27,381
Only an interval entirely below that threshold rules out
the programme's worthwhile benefit at that exposure.

21
00:01:27,381 --> 00:01:30,990
These are proposed research rules, not clinical
thresholds.

22
00:01:34,333 --> 00:01:39,765
The offline navigator links genes to candidate conditions
and shows each source's association role.

23
00:01:39,765 --> 00:01:47,451
Twenty-eight selected queries passed, with complete review
of every returned source association: forty-seven gene and
register-row pairs.

24
00:01:47,451 --> 00:01:53,486
This was a developer evaluation using the same source
snapshots, not independent clinical validation.

25
00:01:53,486 --> 00:01:57,076
All register rows remain visible, including unmapped
entries.

26
00:01:57,076 --> 00:01:59,406
A match does not establish eligibility.

27
00:01:59,406 --> 00:02:00,936
Queries stay on the device.

28
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:08,459
We implemented these rescue-decision rules as a research
software prototype.

29
00:02:08,459 --> 00:02:18,156
All forty frozen synthetic cases matched their expected
decisions, including protein-only signals, selective
killing, missing data and confidence-boundary cases.

30
00:02:18,156 --> 00:02:21,915
This verifies software behaviour, not biological rescue.

31
00:02:21,915 --> 00:02:25,703
Separately, real Splice A I inference passes six controls.

32
00:02:25,703 --> 00:02:28,254
Its checker rejects nine injected failures.

33
00:02:28,254 --> 00:02:32,856
Laboratory function, exposure and independent replication
remain unmeasured.

34
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:41,332
The next step is a laboratory test of full-length variant
function and exposure-limited rescue.

35
00:02:41,332 --> 00:02:44,781
The proposal says what would advance the candidate and
what would stop it.

36
00:02:44,781 --> 00:02:49,495
The reusable tools, source trail and plain-language
explanation are delivered now.

37
00:02:49,495 --> 00:02:51,478
Clinical benefit remains to be earned.

38
00:02:51,478 --> 00:02:54,147
That is the standard we want this work judged against.
